{
    "background_story": "Lorenzo was a linguist with a passion for obscure languages. He spent years studying the Ubykh language, a Caucasian tongue once spoken in the northwestern Caucasus region. Fascinated by its complex grammar and unique sound system, Lorenzo became one of the world's leading experts on Ubykh. He traveled to the Caucasus to learn from the last native speakers, documenting their stories and traditions. Lorenzo's dedication helped preserve the language, which was declared extinct in 1992 with the death of its last fluent speaker, Tevfik Esen\u00e7. However, Lorenzo's work ensured that Ubykh's legacy lived on, inspiring a new generation of scholars and language enthusiasts. His love for this ancient tongue sparked a movement to revive and promote the cultural heritage of the Ubykh people.",
